  "seoBody": "<h2>£20 per active user per month</h2><p>Quickler pricing is £20 per active user per month, with a £20 monthly minimum. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows in that month. One workflow in a month does not make a user active, so a user who does a single report costs nothing. Dormant users are free, so you can add every engineer, manager and admin in your firm and only pay for the people who actually worked. Billed monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit. No setup fee.</p><h2>Free tier</h2><p>There is no time-limited trial. The free tier is how you try quickler: 20 reports a month, with up to 10 photos per report, free forever. Sign up with no card. You only add a Direct Debit when you upgrade to a paid account because you have outgrown the free reports.</p><h2>Why only active users and not per seat</h2><p>Most inspection software charges per seat, which means you pay for every name on the account whether they use it or not. Quickler only charges for users who completed at least two workflows that month, so a firm with twenty occasional users pays only for the handful who worked. Here is the full reasoning on <a href=\"/pages/no-subscription-compliance.html\">only charging for active users</a>.</p><h2>Bigger teams and other countries</h2><p>Big team? <a href=\"mailto:hello@quickler.co\">Talk to us</a>. Rooted in UK compliance, <a href=\"/pages/global-field-compliance.html\">Quickler works in any country</a> WhatsApp does, starting with the UK and reaching English-speaking markets including Ireland, the United States, Canada, Australia and New Zealand.</p>",
